.TH PANTEXT 1
.SH NAME
pantext \- the text layer slides within its grid
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/pantext
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I PanText
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/PanText.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Six sweeps of thirty milliseconds a step: the text slides right by seven
pixels, back through zero to minus seven, and home again, then the same
vertically.  TempleOS composites a character layer over the graphics
layer on a fixed 8x8 grid, and two globals shift that layer by up to a
whole cell, which is how text scrolls smoothly over a grid that cannot
itself move.
.PP
There is no separate character layer here, so the port draws its text at
the offset instead.  The motion is the same; in the original everything
already on screen moves, not only what this program drew.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/pantext.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
